    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as our premier option with a score of 65.95. His matchup against Sonny Gray is favorable, as the combination of a high-impact park factor (+10%) and a strong platoon advantage (+13%) significantly elevates his floor. While our other starters hover in the marginal-to-strong range, **Cal Raleigh** remains a critical piece at 59.42; he benefits from wind blowing out (+5%), which helps mitigate the concern of facing a tough arm like Sasaki, who carries a solid 4.11 xERA. **Luis Arraez** and **Masyn Winn** are both reliable starts, buoyed by favorable pitching matchups that keep them comfortably above our 50-point threshold for daily efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day involved **Braden Montgomery**, who finished just shy of the lineup with a score of 36.72. While his switch-hitting versatility is a nice asset, he was relegated to the bench primarily due to a challenging matchup against Weathers, whose 3.41 xERA suppressed **Braden Montgomery**\u2019s projection below our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. We are opting to prioritize the higher-upside platoon edges of **Jonathan Aranda** and **JJ Bleday** to maximize our daily scoring potential, though **JJ Bleday** remains a riskier play given his -14% platoon penalty against Ram\u00edrez. \n\nWith **Will Smith** still sidelined on the IL, we continue to rely on the depth of our bench to mitigate volatility. We are monitoring all lineups closely for any last-minute weather shifts, but as it stands, our current configuration provides the best balance of plate appearances and matchup advantages. We are avoiding exposure to top-tier arms where possible, as the current rotation of starters represents the most efficient path to securing Roto gains today without exhausting our game caps on sub-optimal matchups.",
